The legal text is the Constitution of the Republic of Vanuatu, Consolidated English Version (Laws of the
Republic of Vanuatu, Consolidated Edition 2020, "Order commenced on 29th April 2020"), as published by the
Parliament of the Republic of Vanuatu:

  Source: https://parliament.gov.vu/images/constitution.pdf, retrieved 30 October 2026.

The Parliament's website states no terms of reuse for this text (its robots.txt is absent and its
"Terms & Conditions" page is missing), and Vanuatu's Copyright and Related Rights Act No. 42 of 2000
has no clause excluding legislation from protection. The text is reproduced unchanged as the official
publication of the nation's supreme law, with attribution to the Parliament of Vanuatu. If the Parliament
or the Government of Vanuatu asks for its removal, it will be removed.

Changes made by Lexifina: the text layer of the PDF was converted to one Markdown file per article;
page headers and page numbers were removed; broken dash glyphs were normalised; and wrapped lines were
joined into paragraphs. No model wrote or edited any legal text.

The tools, README and other material added by Lexifina are released under CC0 1.0.
